IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g5-art13-reporting`
IMPORT `g5-tests-fixtures`

-- g5-tests-art13-reporting.l4: tests of Article 13(6) to (10) and (12).  Every expected value was decided from the Law's text (quoted above each
-- group) before the run.  A DEONTIC has no equality, so each regulative rule is run with #TRACE and the expectation sits in an EXPECT comment right
-- above the trace (checked by check-traces.py): FULFILLED, BREACH or STANDING (the rule is printed back, still open).

§ `Tests of Article 13 (effects of registration), paragraphs (6) to (10) and (12)`

§§ `Readings and cases used below`

`the favoured reading` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`

-- A matter that arose on 1 March 2026, of which the charity became aware on 20 March 2026.
`the timing of the March matter` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 3 20

`a report made on 15 March 2026` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 15)
    `the report was made promptly` IS TRUE

`a report made on 16 March 2026` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 16)
    `the report was made promptly` IS TRUE

`a report made on 25 March 2026` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 25)
    `the report was made promptly` IS TRUE

`a report made on 3 April 2026` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 4 3)
    `the report was made promptly` IS TRUE

`a report made on 4 April 2026` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 4 4)
    `the report was made promptly` IS TRUE

`no report has been made` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS NOTHING
    `the report was made promptly` IS FALSE

`a report judged prompt` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 9 1)
    `the report was made promptly` IS TRUE

`a report judged not prompt` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 9 1)
    `the report was made promptly` IS FALSE

§§ `Article 13(6): the matters to report`

-- src:383 | (6) A registered charity must promptly report to the Commissioner –
-- src:384 | (a) a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register (whether in the general or restricted section) in relation to that charity;
@ref Article 13 (src:383-384)
`a changed registered matter` MEANS `a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register` TRUE TRUE
`an unchanged registered matter` MEANS `a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register` TRUE FALSE
`a changed matter not on the register` MEANS `a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register` FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `an unchanged registered matter`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed matter not on the register`

-- src:385 | (b) any other matter, coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name, that could, if known before the registration or permission, have led to the Commissioner refusing to register the charity, refusing to accept the name of the charity, or entering it in a different section;
@ref Article 13 (src:385)
-- Arguments of the constructor: came to light after registration or permission; could have led to refusal to register; could have led to a different section.
`a later matter that could have led to refusal` MEANS `a matter coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a later matter that could have led to a different section` MEANS `a matter coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name` TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a later matter that would have made no difference` MEANS `a matter coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`an earlier matter that could have led to refusal` MEANS `a matter coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name` FALSE TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a later matter that could have led to refusal`
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a later matter that could have led to a different section`
-- The third limb, "refusing to accept the name of the charity", is Article 12(1): the name is undesirable (integration point IP18).
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a later matter that would have made no difference`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a later matter that would have made no difference`
-- A matter known before registration is not one that came to light after it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `an earlier matter that could have led to refusal`

-- src:386 | (c) a proposal to change the charity’s constitution;
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a proposal to change the charity's constitution` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a proposal to change the charity's constitution` FALSE)

-- src:387 | (d) a proposal that could result, or an event that has resulted in the charity ceasing to meet the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d);
@ref Article 13 (src:387)
-- Arguments of the constructor: a proposal that could result in ceasing to meet them; an event has occurred that has resulted in ceasing.
`a proposal that could end the Jersey activity` MEANS `a proposal or an event affecting the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)` TRUE FALSE
`an event that has ended the principal address` MEANS `a proposal or an event affecting the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)` FALSE TRUE
`neither a proposal nor an event` MEANS `a proposal or an event affecting the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)` FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a proposal that could end the Jersey activity`
-- An event counts only if it has in fact resulted in the charity ceasing to meet (c) or (d): (c) no longer met, or (d) no longer met.
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` FALSE TRUE FALSE `an event that has ended the principal address`
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE FALSE FALSE `an event that has ended the principal address`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `an event that has ended the principal address`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `neither a proposal nor an event`

-- src:388 | (e) a reportable matter, in relation to a governor of the charity, if the charity is aware that the governor has not promptly reported it to the Commissioner under Article 19(2);
@ref Article 13 (src:388)
`Bob's reportable matter, the charity aware` MEANS `a reportable matter in relation to a governor` "Bob Renouf" TRUE
`Bob's reportable matter, the charity not aware` MEANS `a reportable matter in relation to a governor` "Bob Renouf" FALSE
`Alice, who has no reportable matter, the charity aware` MEANS `a reportable matter in relation to a governor` "Alice Le Brun" TRUE
`a stranger's reportable matter, the charity aware` MEANS `a reportable matter in relation to a governor` "Carol Ahier" TRUE

#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `Bob's reportable matter, the charity aware`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `Bob's reportable matter, the charity not aware`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `Alice, who has no reportable matter, the charity aware`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a stranger's reportable matter, the charity aware`

-- src:389 | (f) a matter likely to lead to the charity becoming bankrupt, being wound up or otherwise ceasing to exist;
-- src:390 | (g) if the charity is entered in the restricted section, a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets a condition prescribed under Article 9(2); and
-- src:391 | (h) any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a matter likely to lead to bankruptcy, winding up or ceasing to exist` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a matter likely to lead to bankruptcy, winding up or ceasing to exist` FALSE)
-- (g) is for a charity entered in the restricted section only.
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust, in the restricted section` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets its restricted-section condition` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets its restricted-section condition` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust, in the restricted section` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets its restricted-section condition` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a matter prescribed by Order under Article 13(6)(h)` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a matter prescribed by Order under Article 13(6)(h)` FALSE)

§§ `Article 13(6): "promptly" (fork F5.1) and counting the days (fork F5.10)`

-- src:383 | (6) A registered charity must promptly report to the Commissioner –
-- Reading A (taken): promptness is an input judgement.
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` `the favoured reading` `the timing of the March matter` `a report judged prompt`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` `the favoured reading` `the timing of the March matter` `a report judged not prompt`
-- Discriminating case (event 1 March, awareness 20 March, report 25 March, 14 days): late if counted from the event, prompt if from awareness.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) `the timing of the March matter` `a report made on 25 March 2026`
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from awareness in` 14) `the timing of the March matter` `a report made on 25 March 2026`
-- The edge: the last prompt day is the event day plus 14 (15 March), the day of the event not being counted.
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) `the timing of the March matter` `a report made on 15 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) `the timing of the March matter` `a report made on 16 March 2026`
-- Counted from awareness (20 March plus 14 is 3 April).
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from awareness in` 14) `the timing of the March matter` `a report made on 3 April 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from awareness in` 14) `the timing of the March matter` `a report made on 4 April 2026`
-- No report: not prompt on a count of days.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made`
-- Fork F5.10, reading B: the day of the event is the first day, so the last prompt day is 14 March.
#ASSERT `F5.10 A: the last prompt day when the day of the event is not counted` (YMD 2026 3 1) 14 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `F5.10 B: the last prompt day when the day of the event is the first day` (YMD 2026 3 1) 14 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the last prompt day` `the favoured reading` (YMD 2026 3 1) 14 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the last prompt day` `the interpretation with the day of the event as day one` (YMD 2026 3 1) 14 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness from the event in` 14) `the timing of the March matter` `a report made on 15 March 2026`

§§ `Article 13(6): the duty as a regulative rule`

-- The duty binds a registered charity, and only as to a matter within a paragraph of (6).
-- Reading A: promptness is an input; an act of reporting counts as performance only if it was prompt; otherwise the duty stands.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` `the favoured reading` TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `a report judged prompt` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `report a matter to the Commissioner` `a changed registered matter` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` `the favoured reading` TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `a report judged not prompt` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `report a matter to the Commissioner` `a changed registered matter` AT 5

-- A matter that falls within no paragraph: nothing to report.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` `the favoured reading` TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `an unchanged registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Not a registered charity: the duty does not bind.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` `the favoured reading` FALSE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Reading B (14 days from the event, 1 March 2026): a report on 15 March is in time, on 16 March is not.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `report a matter to the Commissioner` `a changed registered matter` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 15))

-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(6)
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `report a matter to the Commissioner` `a changed registered matter` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 16))

-- A matter never reported: the clock passes the last prompt day.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(6)
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 16)))

-- Reading C (14 days from awareness, 20 March 2026): a report on 3 April is in time, on 4 April is not.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from awareness in` 14) TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `report a matter to the Commissioner` `a changed registered matter` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 4 3))

-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(6)
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from awareness in` 14) TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `report a matter to the Commissioner` `a changed registered matter` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 4 4))

-- Fork F5.10, reading B (the day of the event is day one): 15 March is already late.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(6)
#TRACE `Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` (`the interpretation with promptness from the event in` 14) TRUE `the Arts Trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a changed registered matter` `the timing of the March matter` `no report has been made` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `report a matter to the Commissioner` `a changed registered matter` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 3 15))

§§ `Article 13(7): the year to which the return relates (fork F5.2), and the anniversary on 29 February (fork F5.11)`

-- src:392 | (7) A registered charity must send an annual return to the Commissioner, containing information as to any matter falling within paragraph (6) arising during the year to which the return relates, and as to any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
@ref Article 13 (src:392)
`a day in the autumn of 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 12 1
`a day in the winter of 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 2 10

-- Reading A (taken): the calendar year.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the autumn of 2026` EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31)
-- Reading B: the charity's financial year, ending on 30 June.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` (JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 6, 30)) `a day in the autumn of 2026` EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 7 1), (YMD 2027 6 30)
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` (JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 6, 30)) `a day in the winter of 2026` EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2025 7 1), (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- The year-end day itself is the last day of its financial year; the next day begins the next.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` (JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 6, 30)) (YMD 2026 6 30) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2025 7 1), (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` (JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 6, 30)) (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 7 1), (YMD 2027 6 30)
-- A financial year that ends on 31 December is the calendar year.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` (JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 12, 31)) `a day in the autumn of 2026` EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31)
-- Reading B needs the financial year end; with none given the question is a named refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the autumn of 2026` BECAUSE "the financial year end of the charity is not given, so the financial year cannot be found"
-- Reading C: the twelve months from each anniversary of registration (registered 1 March 2019).
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the winter of 2026` EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2025 3 1), (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2027 2 28)
-- The first year runs to the day before the second anniversary, 29 February 2020 being a day of it.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING (YMD 2019 3 1) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2019 3 1), (YMD 2020 2 29)
-- A day before the charity was registered is in no year of its return.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING (YMD 2019 2 28) BECAUSE "the reference day is before the charity was registered, so it is in no year of the charity's return"
-- Fork F5.11: a charity registered on 29 February 2020, and the reference day 28 February 2025.
-- Reading A (taken): the anniversary in 2025 is 28 February, so 28 February 2025 begins a year.  Reading B: the anniversary is 1 March 2025, so 28 February 2025 ends the year that began on 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `F5.11 A: the anniversary clamped to the last day of the month` (YMD 2020 2 29) 5 EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `F5.11 B: the anniversary rolled forward` (YMD 2020 2 29) 5 EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1
#ASSERT `F5.11 A: the anniversary clamped to the last day of the month` (YMD 2020 2 29) 4 EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `F5.11 B: the anniversary rolled forward` (YMD 2020 2 29) 4 EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the leap day charity` NOTHING (YMD 2025 2 28) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2025 2 28), (YMD 2026 2 27)
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration and 29 February rolled` `the leap day charity` NOTHING (YMD 2025 2 28) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2024 2 29), (YMD 2025 2 28)

§§ `Article 13(7): what the annual return must contain (and fork F5.13: when a matter arises)`

-- Matters of the Arts Trust, calendar year 2026.  Fields: reference; falls within paragraph (6); timing; the return gives information about it.
`a matter of 2026 reported in the return` MEANS `Matter arising for the annual return` WITH
    reference IS "change of trustee"
    `falls within paragraph (6)` IS TRUE
    timing IS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 5 5, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 5 6
    `the annual return gives information about it` IS TRUE

`a matter of 2026 left out of the return` MEANS `Matter arising for the annual return` WITH
    reference IS "proposal to change the constitution"
    `falls within paragraph (6)` IS TRUE
    timing IS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 7 1, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 7 1
    `the annual return gives information about it` IS FALSE

`a matter of 2025 left out of the return` MEANS `Matter arising for the annual return` WITH
    reference IS "an old change of address"
    `falls within paragraph (6)` IS TRUE
    timing IS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2025 11 30, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2025 11 30
    `the annual return gives information about it` IS FALSE

`a matter outside paragraph (6) left out of the return` MEANS `Matter arising for the annual return` WITH
    reference IS "a routine purchase"
    `falls within paragraph (6)` IS FALSE
    timing IS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 8 8, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 8 8
    `the annual return gives information about it` IS FALSE

-- An event on 30 December 2026 of which the charity became aware on 5 January 2027 (fork F5.13).
`a matter that arose in December 2026 and came to the charity's notice in January 2027` MEANS `Matter arising for the annual return` WITH
    reference IS "an event at the year end"
    `falls within paragraph (6)` IS TRUE
    timing IS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 12 30, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2027 1 5
    `the annual return gives information about it` IS FALSE

`the calendar year 2026` MEANS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31)

`the timing of a matter on 1-1-2026` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 1 1
`the timing of a matter on 31-12-2026` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 12 31, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 12 31
`the timing of a matter on 31-12-2025` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2025 12 31, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2025 12 31
`the timing of a matter on 1-1-2027` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2027 1 1

#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the annual return contains the information paragraph (7) requires` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a matter of 2026 reported in the return`, `a matter of 2025 left out of the return`, `a matter outside paragraph (6) left out of the return`) TRUE
-- A matter within paragraph (6) that arose in the year and is not in the return: the return is incomplete.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(7) the annual return contains the information paragraph (7) requires` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a matter of 2026 reported in the return`, `a matter of 2026 left out of the return`) TRUE
-- The other matters prescribed by an Order are required too.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(7) the annual return contains the information paragraph (7) requires` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a matter of 2026 reported in the return`) FALSE
-- No matters at all: only the prescribed matters can be missing.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the annual return contains the information paragraph (7) requires` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` EMPTY TRUE
-- Boundary days of the year.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` `the timing of a matter on 1-1-2026`
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` `the timing of a matter on 31-12-2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` `the timing of a matter on 31-12-2025`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` `the timing of a matter on 1-1-2027`
-- Fork F5.13: reading A (taken), the matter arose when the event happened (December 2026), so it belongs to the 2026 return; reading B, when the charity became aware (January 2027).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(7) the annual return contains the information paragraph (7) requires` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a matter that arose in December 2026 and came to the charity's notice in January 2027`) TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the annual return contains the information paragraph (7) requires` `the interpretation with the date of awareness` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a matter that arose in December 2026 and came to the charity's notice in January 2027`) TRUE

§§ `Article 13(7) and (8): the duty to send the annual return, its due date, lateness (forks F5.5)`

-- src:393 | (8) An Order under paragraph (7) may also make provision as to the format and timing of the annual return, the consequences of lateness, and the content of any entries to be made on the register in respect of the annual return.
@ref Article 13 (src:393)
`an Order with no due date and no consequence` MEANS `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` WITH
    `due date of the annual return` IS NOTHING
    `consequence of lateness` IS NOTHING

`an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` MEANS `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` WITH
    `due date of the annual return` IS JUST (YMD 2027 3 31)
    `consequence of lateness` IS JUST "a late fee of 50 pounds"

-- Reading A (taken): sent on the due date is timely.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 1 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `send the annual return to the Commissioner` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 3 31))

-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(7)
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 1 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `send the annual return to the Commissioner` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 4 1))

-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(7)
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 1 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 4 1)))

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 1 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `send the annual return to the Commissioner` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 3 30))

-- Reading B (fork F5.5): the return must be sent before the due date, so 31 March is already late.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(7)
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the interpretation with a return due before the due date` TRUE `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 1 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `send the annual return to the Commissioner` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 3 31))

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the interpretation with a return due before the due date` TRUE `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 1 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `send the annual return to the Commissioner` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 3 30))

-- No Order fixes a due date: the Law states no time, so the duty stands however long the clock runs.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an Order with no due date and no consequence` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 100000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an Order with no due date and no consequence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `send the annual return to the Commissioner` AT 100000

-- An entity that is not a registered charity is not bound.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `the favoured reading` FALSE `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 1 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 4 30)))

-- Lateness.  Reading A: sent on the due date is not late; the day after is.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the favoured reading` `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` (YMD 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the favoured reading` `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` (YMD 2027 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the favoured reading` `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` (YMD 2027 3 30)
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the interpretation with a return due before the due date` `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` (YMD 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the interpretation with a return due before the due date` `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` (YMD 2027 3 30)
-- With no Order the Law fixes no due date: a refusal, not FALSE.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the favoured reading` `an Order with no due date and no consequence` (YMD 2027 4 1) BECAUSE "no Order under Article 13(8) fixing the due date of the annual return is encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) the consequence of lateness` `an Order due on 31 March 2027 with a late fee` EQUALS "a late fee of 50 pounds"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 13(8) the consequence of lateness` `an Order with no due date and no consequence` BECAUSE "no Order under Article 13(8) stating the consequences of lateness is encoded in this model"

