§§ `Article 13(9): payments to a governor, and the Order that requires them`

-- src:394 | (9) The Minister may by Order –
-- src:395 | (a) require a registered charity to include in its annual return details of a prescribed description of any payment made, during the year to which the return relates, by or on behalf of the registered charity to a governor, or to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor;
-- src:396 | (b) require a registered charity to provide to the Commissioner a statement of its current intentions as to making any payments of such a prescribed description in future;
-- src:397 | (c) provide for the entry on the register by the Commissioner of the details included under sub-paragraph (a) in the charity’s latest annual return, and of the statement provided under sub-paragraph (b).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(a) the Minister may by Order require payment details in the annual return` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make an Order` `the details of payments to a governor that an annual return must include, Article 13(9)(a)` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(a) the Minister may by Order require payment details in the annual return` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(b) the Minister may by Order require a statement of intentions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make an Order` `the statement of current intentions as to payments to a governor, Article 13(9)(b)` AT 5

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(c) the Minister may by Order provide for entry on the register` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make an Order` `the entry on the register of those details and of that statement, Article 13(9)(c)` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(c) the Minister may by Order provide for entry on the register` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

`an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` MEANS `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH
    `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS TRUE
    `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS TRUE
    `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS TRUE

`an Order under Article 13(9) requiring only a statement` MEANS `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH
    `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS FALSE
    `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS TRUE
    `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS FALSE

`an Order under Article 13(9) requiring nothing` MEANS `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH
    `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS FALSE
    `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS FALSE
    `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS FALSE

-- A payment of 10 February 2026 by the charity to a governor, of the prescribed description.
`a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH
    description IS "a consultancy fee of 12,000 pounds"
    `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 2 10
    `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a governor of the charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS FALSE
    `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS TRUE
    `the annual return gives its details` IS FALSE

`a payment to a connected person on 10 February 2026` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH
    description IS "rent of 9,000 pounds to a governor's spouse"
    `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 2 10
    `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a governor of the charity` IS FALSE
    `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS TRUE
    `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS TRUE
    `the annual return gives its details` IS FALSE

`a payment to an outsider on 10 February 2026` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH
    description IS "a supplier's invoice"
    `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 2 10
    `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a governor of the charity` IS FALSE
    `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS FALSE
    `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS TRUE
    `the annual return gives its details` IS FALSE

`a payment to a governor not of the prescribed description` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH
    description IS "a payment of a kind the Order does not describe"
    `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 2 10
    `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a governor of the charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS FALSE
    `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS FALSE
    `the annual return gives its details` IS FALSE

`a payment to a governor by someone else` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH
    description IS "a gift from a donor"
    `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 2 10
    `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS FALSE
    `made to a governor of the charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS FALSE
    `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS TRUE
    `the annual return gives its details` IS FALSE

`the financial year 2026-27 of a charity with a 30 June year end` MEANS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 7 1), (YMD 2027 6 30)

#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` `a payment to a connected person on 10 February 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` `a payment to an outsider on 10 February 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` `a payment to a governor not of the prescribed description`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` `a payment to a governor by someone else`
-- No Order applies, or the Order does not require details in the return: nothing to include.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` FALSE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring only a statement` `the calendar year 2026` `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`
-- The year: a payment on 10 February 2026 is in the return for the calendar year 2026 and in the financial year 2025-26, and not in the financial year 2026-27.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the financial year 2026-27 of a charity with a 30 June year end` `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` (JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 6, 30)) `a day in the winter of 2026`) `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`
-- Fork F5.2 discriminating case: for the return that covers 1 December 2026, a payment of 10 February 2026 is in it on the calendar-year reading, and not on the financial-year reading.
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the autumn of 2026`) `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` (JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 6, 30)) `a day in the autumn of 2026`) `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`
-- Boundary days of the year.
`a payment to a governor on 31-12-2026` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH description IS "x", `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 12 31, `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS TRUE, `made to a governor of the charity` IS TRUE, `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS FALSE, `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS TRUE, `the annual return gives its details` IS FALSE
`a payment to a governor on 1-1-2027` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH description IS "x", `date of the payment` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS TRUE, `made to a governor of the charity` IS TRUE, `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS FALSE, `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS TRUE, `the annual return gives its details` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` `a payment to a governor on 31-12-2026` `the calendar year 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` `a payment to a governor on 1-1-2027` `the calendar year 2026`

-- A payment the return does give details of (field: the annual return gives its details).
`a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026, given in the return` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH
    description IS "a consultancy fee of 12,000 pounds"
    `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 2 10
    `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a governor of the charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS FALSE
    `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS TRUE
    `the annual return gives its details` IS TRUE

-- The annual return of a charity to which an Order under 13(9)(a) applies must give the details of every payment that falls to be included.
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the annual return gives the details of the payments the Order requires` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026, given in the return`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the annual return gives the details of the payments the Order requires` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`)
-- A payment that does not fall to be included (an outsider, or outside the year) need not be in the return; so a return that omits it is complete.
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the annual return gives the details of the payments the Order requires` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026, given in the return`, `a payment to an outsider on 10 February 2026`, `a payment to a governor on 1-1-2027`)
-- No Order applies: nothing to give.
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the annual return gives the details of the payments the Order requires` FALSE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` (LIST `a payment to a governor on 10 February 2026`)
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the annual return gives the details of the payments the Order requires` TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` `the calendar year 2026` EMPTY

-- (b): once an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, it must provide the statement.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(b) the registered charity must provide a statement of its current intentions` TRUE TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `provide the Commissioner with a statement of current intentions as to payments to a governor` AT 40

-- The Law states no time and the Order's is not in the sources, so the duty stands however long the clock runs.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(b) the registered charity must provide a statement of its current intentions` TRUE TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 100000)

-- An Order that does not require a statement, an Order that does not apply to the charity (relieved), or an entity that is not a registered charity: no duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(b) the registered charity must provide a statement of its current intentions` TRUE TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring nothing` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 100000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(b) the registered charity must provide a statement of its current intentions` TRUE FALSE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 100000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(9)(b) the registered charity must provide a statement of its current intentions` FALSE TRUE `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 100000)

§§ `Article 13(10): relief for small charities; integration point IP29`

-- src:398 | (10) The Minister may by Order, after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities, provide that any provision of paragraph (6) or (7), or of any Order under paragraph (7), (8) or (9) –
-- src:399 | (a) does not apply to a prescribed description of charity appearing to the Minister to require relief from the burden of that provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of charities of that description; or
-- src:400 | (b) applies to a prescribed description of charity only subject to a modification prescribed by the Order, being a modification that appears to the Minister to give reasonable relief from the burden of that provision, having regard to the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of charities of that description.
@ref Article 13 (src:398-400)
-- Fields of a relief Order: the provision it names; the relief; the Minister consulted the Commissioner; consulted a representative body; it appears to the Minister that relief is needed; the charity is of the prescribed description.
`a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), for the charity's description` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of paragraph (7)`
    relief IS `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

`a relief Order that was made without consulting the Commissioner` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of paragraph (7)`
    relief IS `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS FALSE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

`a relief Order that was made without consulting a representative body` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of paragraph (7)`
    relief IS `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS FALSE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

`a relief Order made though it does not appear to the Minister that relief is needed` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of paragraph (7)`
    relief IS `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS FALSE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

`a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), but the charity is not of the description` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of paragraph (7)`
    relief IS `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS FALSE

`a valid relief Order by modification from paragraph (6)` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of paragraph (6)`
    relief IS `relief by modification, Article 13(10)(b)` "an annual report on every matter, in place of a prompt report"
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

`a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (8)` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)`
    relief IS `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

`a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (7)` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7)`
    relief IS `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

`a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (9)` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)`
    relief IS `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

`a valid relief Order by modification naming an Order under paragraph (9)` MEANS `Order under Article 13(10)` WITH
    provision IS `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)`
    relief IS `relief by modification, Article 13(10)(b)` "a statement once a year in place of each time"
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS TRUE
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS TRUE
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS TRUE

-- The power: open only after both consultations and on the Minister's opinion.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` `a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), for the charity's description`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` `a relief Order that was made without consulting the Commissioner`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` `a relief Order that was made without consulting a representative body`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` `a relief Order made though it does not appear to the Minister that relief is needed`

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order relieve small charities` `a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), for the charity's description` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make an Order` `relief for a prescribed description of charity, Article 13(10)` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order relieve small charities` `a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), for the charity's description` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Without the consultation there is no permission.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order relieve small charities` `a relief Order that was made without consulting the Commissioner` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- The effect of a valid Order (a): the provision does not apply to a charity of the description.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), for the charity's description` `a provision of paragraph (7)` EQUALS `the provision does not apply to the charity`
-- ... but only the provision it names.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), for the charity's description` `a provision of paragraph (6)` EQUALS `the provision applies in full`
-- ... and only for a charity of the prescribed description.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), but the charity is not of the description` `a provision of paragraph (7)` EQUALS `the provision applies in full`
-- An Order made without the consultations, or without the Minister's opinion, has no effect.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a relief Order that was made without consulting the Commissioner` `a provision of paragraph (7)` EQUALS `the provision applies in full`
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a relief Order made though it does not appear to the Minister that relief is needed` `a provision of paragraph (7)` EQUALS `the provision applies in full`
-- (b): applies only subject to the prescribed modification.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a valid relief Order by modification from paragraph (6)` `a provision of paragraph (6)` EQUALS `the provision applies to the charity only subject to a modification` "an annual report on every matter, in place of a prompt report"
-- Fork F5.3 (trap T18): a relief Order that names "an Order under paragraph (8)" and the lateness consequences set by an Order under paragraph (7) by virtue of paragraph (8).
-- Reading A (taken): the Order under (8) is the Order under (7) as extended, so the relief reaches them.  Reading B (literal): there is no Order under (8), so the relief reaches nothing.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)` EQUALS `the provision does not apply to the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the interpretation with no Order under paragraph (8)` `a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)` EQUALS `the provision applies in full`
-- An Order naming "an Order under paragraph (7)" reaches the (8) provisions on either reading, since they are provisions of an Order under (7).
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (7)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)` EQUALS `the provision does not apply to the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the interpretation with no Order under paragraph (8)` `a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (7)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)` EQUALS `the provision does not apply to the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (7)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) not made by virtue of paragraph (8)` EQUALS `the provision does not apply to the charity`
-- On reading A an Order naming (8) reaches only the (8) provisions, not the rest of the Order under (7).
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the favoured reading` `a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) not made by virtue of paragraph (8)` EQUALS `the provision applies in full`
#ASSERT `F5.3 A: the Order under paragraph (8) is the Order under paragraph (7) as extended` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)`
#ASSERT NOT `F5.3 B: no Order exists under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)`

-- IP29: does an Order under Article 13(9) apply to the charity?
#ASSERT `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the favoured reading` (JUST `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three`) EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the favoured reading` (JUST `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring only a statement`) EMPTY
-- An Order that requires and provides nothing is no Order that applies; with no Order encoded it does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the favoured reading` (JUST `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring nothing`) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the favoured reading` NOTHING EMPTY
-- Relief by disapplication of a provision of an Order under (9) for a charity of the description takes the charity out of it ...
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the favoured reading` (JUST `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three`) (LIST `a valid relief Order naming an Order under paragraph (9)`)
-- ... but a relief Order that is invalid, or names another provision, or is for another description, or only modifies, leaves it applying.
#ASSERT `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the favoured reading` (JUST `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three`) (LIST `a relief Order that was made without consulting the Commissioner`)
#ASSERT `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the favoured reading` (JUST `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three`) (LIST `a valid relief Order from paragraph (7), for the charity's description`)
#ASSERT `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the favoured reading` (JUST `an Order under Article 13(9) requiring all three`) (LIST `a valid relief Order by modification naming an Order under paragraph (9)`)

§§ `Article 13(12): Regulations under Article 11(7)`

-- src:404 | (12) If the States make Regulations under Article 11(7), those Regulations may also make provision requiring a registered charity or its governors (or both) to avoid, or report and remedy, a situation arising at a time after registration, being a situation in which, if the charity were at that time applying for registration, there would be grounds under those Regulations to refuse that application.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(12) the States may require a charity to avoid or report and remedy a later ground for refusal` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the States` DOES `make Regulations requiring a charity or its governors to avoid, or report and remedy, a later ground for refusal` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 13(12) the States may require a charity to avoid or report and remedy a later ground for refusal` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- No Regulations under Article 11(7): no further power under paragraph (12).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(12) the States may require a charity to avoid or report and remedy a later ground for refusal` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

#ASSERT `Art 13(12) the situation is one the Regulations may require the charity or its governors to avoid or to report and remedy` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(12) the situation is one the Regulations may require the charity or its governors to avoid or to report and remedy` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(12) the situation is one the Regulations may require the charity or its governors to avoid or to report and remedy` TRUE FALSE
